# Most of what Claude Code writes into .claude is local state: worktrees, lock files and
# settings.local.json. The vendored skills are the tracked exception, and they are the whole
# point of the directory being tracked at all. Anything else under .claude that is meant to be
# shared needs its own negation below.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills
